%N A364047 Expansion of Sum_{k>0} x^k / (1 + x^(6*k)).
%C A364047 In general, if m>=1 and g.f. = Sum_{k>=1} x^k / (1 + x^(m*k)) then Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ n * Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^k/(m*k + 1) = n * (PolyGamma(0, 1/2 + 1/(2*m)) - PolyGamma(0, 1/(2*m)))/(2*m). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 20 2026
%H A364047 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A364047/b364047.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A364047 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A364047/a364047.jpg">Plot of Sum_{k=1..n} a(k)/n for n = 1..10^8</a>
%F A364047 G.f.: Sum_{k>0} (-1)^(k-1) * x^(6*k-5) / (1 - x^(6*k-5)).
%F A364047 a(n) = Sum_{d|n, d==1 (mod 6)} (-1)^((d-1)/6).
%F A364047 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ (Pi/6 + log(2 + sqrt(3)) / (2*sqrt(3))) * n. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 20 2026
%t A364047 a[n_] := DivisorSum[n, (-1)^((#-1)/6) &, Mod[#, 6] == 1 &]; Array[a, 100] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 03 2023 *)
%o A364047 (PARI) a(n) = sumdiv(n, d, (d%6==1)*(-1)^((d-1)/6));
%Y A364047 Cf. A048272, A002654, A364011, A363037, A364043.
